.TH "CSSNUMERICARRAY" "3JS" "August 15, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSNumericArray \- CSSNumericArray
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSNumericArray\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed
Object Model API represents an iterable of
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R]\-based objects.
.PP
An object of this type is used to represent the operands of a
mathematical operation in the \f[CR]values\f[R] property of
\f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R], \f[CR]CSSMathProduct\f[R], \f[CR]CSSMathMin\f[R],
and \f[CR]CSSMathMax\f[R].
.PP
The items can be accessed by index (\f[CR]array[0]\f[R]), and as an
iterable it can be used with a \f[CR]for...of\f[R] loop or the spread
syntax.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]CSSNumericArray.length\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns the number of items in the object.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
.TP
\f[B]CSSNumericArray.entries()\f[R]
Returns a new \f[I]array iterator\f[R] that yields
\f[CR][index, value]\f[R] pairs for each item in the object.
.TP
\f[B]CSSNumericArray.forEach()\f[R]
Executes a provided function once for each item in the object.
.TP
\f[B]CSSNumericArray.keys()\f[R]
Returns a new \f[I]array iterator\f[R] that yields the index of each
item in the object.
.TP
\f[B]CSSNumericArray.values()\f[R]
Returns a new \f[I]array iterator\f[R] that yields each item in the
object.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Reading the terms of a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R]
The \f[CR]values\f[R] property of a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] is a
\f[CR]CSSNumericArray\f[R] containing the terms of the sum.
This example creates a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R], then reads its
\f[CR]values\f[R] via \f[CR]length\f[R], indexed access, and iteration.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] sum = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSMathSum(CSS.px(10), CSS.em(5), CSS.percent(50));
\f[B]const\f[R] values = sum.values;

console.log(values.length); \f[I]// 3\f[R]
console.log(values[0]); \f[I]// CSSUnitValue {value: 10, unit: \(dqpx\(dq}\f[R]

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] value \f[B]of\f[R] values) {
  console.log(value.toString());
}
\f[I]// \(dq10px\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// \(dq5em\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// \(dq50%\(dq\f[R]
.EE
